### Prerequisites

- [X] I understand and accept the project's [code of conduct](https://github.com/PrestaShop/PrestaShop/blob/develop/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)
- [X] I have already [searched in existing issues](https://github.com/PrestaShop/PrestaShop/issues?q=is%3Aissue+label%3ABug) and found no previous report of this bug.

### Describe the bug and add screenshots

Since this PR was merged https://github.com/PrestaShop/PrestaShop/pull/26748

The previous code was:
```php
    public static function getHookStatusByName($hook_name): bool
    {
        $sql = new DbQuery();
        $sql->select('active');
        $sql->from('hook', 'h');
        $sql->where('h.name = "' . pSQL($hook_name) . '"');

        return (bool) Db::getInstance()->getValue($sql);
    }
```

Now the code looks like this:

```php
    public static function getHookStatusByName($hook_name): bool
    {
        $hook_names = [];
        if (Cache::isStored('active_hooks')) {
            $hook_names = Cache::retrieve('active_hooks');
        } else {
            $sql = new DbQuery();
            $sql->select('name');
            $sql->from('hook', 'h');
            $sql->where('h.active = 1');
            $active_hooks = Db::getInstance()->executeS($sql);
            if (!empty($active_hooks)) {
                $hook_names = array_column($active_hooks, 'name');
                if (is_array($hook_names)) {
                    Cache::store('active_hooks', $hook_names);
                }
            }
        }

        return in_array($hook_name, $hook_names);
    }
```

The problem is that MySQL is not case sensitive, but `in_array` is.

So if for example in the BDD we have `ModuleRoutes` and in the code `moduleRoutes`
Or `displayOverrideTemplate` in the BDD but `DisplayOverrideTemplate` in the code

Then the hook doesn't trigger, before the modification it used to work.

### Expected behavior

I should be able to trigger hooks with case sensitive inputs and it always work.

### Steps to reproduce

Use the quality inssurance module and try to trigger a hook with different writings (upper/lower cases modifications).
Or identify a hook in the core on which some modules are registered, and modify the spelling of the hook in the core code.

### PrestaShop version(s) where the bug happened

1.7.8.4

### PHP version(s) where the bug happened

Not relevant

